<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1996 nickel output fell 3.0 pct from 1995.</title>
<headline>Russian 1996 nickel output fell 3.0 pct from 1995.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian nickel production fell three percent in 1996 from 1995, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>It released no outright production figures, but gave the following percentage changes for non-ferrous metals and gold output.</p>
<p>	    RUSSIAN 1996 METALS OUTPUT, IN PERCENTAGE CHANGES</p>
<p>     1996 vs 1995    Dec 96 vs Nov 96   1995 vs 1994</p>
<p>aluminium   +3.0		  +3.0	     +4.0</p>
<p> alumina    -5.0		  +0.6	     +15.0</p>
<p> bauxite    +6.0		 +79.0		+2.0</p>
<p> cobalt     -6.0		 +28.0	     +16.0</p>
<p> copper</p>
<p>(refined)   +7.0		  +6.0	     +15.0</p>
<p>(in</p>
<p>concentrate) -0.5		 +5.0	     +6.0</p>
<p>magnesium</p>
<p>and</p>
<p>magnesium    -5.0		 +6.0	     +16.0</p>
<p>nickel	 -3.0		 +6.0	     +19.0</p>
<p>zinc	   +5.0		 -4.0	     +21.0</p>
<p>-- Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
